# Builds signed, verified release APK/AAB assets and publishes them to a
# GitHub Release (replacing the former temporary Actions-artifact upload).
#
# Trigger contract:
#   * Runs ONLY when a pull request targeting `main` is closed AND merged
#     (pull_request types:[closed] + branches:[main] + job-level `if` on
#     github.event.pull_request.merged == true).
#   * A PR closed WITHOUT merging never reaches the build job - no signing,
#     no build, no artifact.
#   * The job checks out the merge commit that landed on main
#     (github.event.pull_request.merge_commit_sha), never PR-head code.
#   * There is NO push trigger and NO workflow_dispatch: signed artifacts are
#     produced only by a merged PR. (workflow_dispatch existed before signing
#     was wired in and was removed here - a manual dispatch would allow
#     on-demand signed builds; re-add only on explicit owner authorization.)
#
# Signing contract:
#   * The Gradle release signing config is env-gated and fail-closed
#     (PB_KEYSTORE_PATH / PB_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD / PB_KEY_ALIAS / PB_KEY_PASSWORD,
#     see signing.env.example and pahebatcher/build.gradle.kts). Unchanged.
#   * This workflow consumes exactly four repository secrets:
#       PB_KEYSTORE_BASE64, PB_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD, PB_KEY_ALIAS, PB_KEY_PASSWORD
#     The keystore is reconstructed from PB_KEYSTORE_BASE64 into RUNNER_TEMP
#     (mode 600) and PB_KEYSTORE_PATH is generated locally - never a secret.
#   * Missing or empty secrets fail the job EARLY with the missing NAME(S)
#     only; no value is ever printed. An incorrectly named secret therefore
#     surfaces as "missing", never as a silent fallback.
#   * Artifact signing is VERIFIED after the build with apksigner/jarsigner
#     (signature validity, signer-certificate consistency across all outputs,
#     per-ABI native-library purity) - Gradle success alone is never trusted.
#   * The AAB integrity gate is `jarsigner -verify` (NON-strict, exit 0
#     required). The release certificate is intentionally self-signed, so
#     `jarsigner -verify -strict` returns exit 4 ("jar verified, with signer
#     errors") for it, while a genuine tamper returns exit 1 in both modes
#     (verified empirically on JDK 25). Keying the gate off the NON-strict
#     result keeps tamper detection (exit 1 still fails) without treating the
#     expected self-signed certificate chain as a failure. The full jarsigner
#     diagnostics are always echoed so the self-signed condition is visible.
#   * The temporary keystore is deleted in an unconditional cleanup step,
#     including after failed builds. It is never uploaded as an artifact.
#
# Job structure (job-level granularity + APK/AAB failure isolation):
#   * THREE independent verification jobs - debug-unit-tests
#     (testDebugUnitTest), release-unit-tests (testReleaseUnitTest) and
#     debug-lint (lintDebug) - gate TWO independent build jobs via `needs:`.
#     All commands and results are visible as separate checks in the Actions
#     UI, and "Re-run failed jobs" reruns only the check that failed (plus its
#     dependents), not the others.
#   * build-apks builds and verifies the two per-ABI release APKs, then hands
#     them to the publishing job. build-aab (needs: build-apks) then builds and
#     verifies the AAB independently. Publication is ALL-OR-NOTHING: the
#     publish-release job `needs:` all five jobs, so an AAB failure blocks the
#     release entirely - there is deliberately NO APK-only publish path.
#   * Every job checks out the SAME merge commit and sets up the same
#     JDK 25 / Android SDK / Gradle toolchain; none of the verification jobs
#     receives any secret. build-apks and build-aab are the only jobs that see
#     signing secrets, and only for a MERGED pull request.
#
# Cross-job handoff (why cache, not actions/upload-artifact):
#   * actions/upload-artifact / actions/download-artifact are NOT used anywhere
#     in this file. The verified files are moved between jobs with
#     actions/cache/save + actions/cache/restore keyed on run id + attempt, so
#     the transfer is a same-run, same-ref transport - NOT a distribution
#     channel. Cache is immutable once saved (no re-write of an existing key),
#     is restored with fail-on-cache-miss, and is re-checksummed in
#     publish-release before anything is published.
#   * Cache, Actions artifacts and release assets are three different things:
#       - Actions artifacts / caches: ephemeral, retention- and
#         quota-governed CI plumbing, not a distribution channel.
#       - GitHub Release assets: the durable, user-facing download surface,
#         served from the repo's Releases page and governed by repository
#         storage/quota limits (release assets are NOT unlimited).
#
# Publication:
#   * publish-release is the ONLY job with `contents: write`; every other job
#     stays read-only. It receives NO signing secret (only the built-in
#     GITHUB_TOKEN, via GH_TOKEN, for `gh`).
#   * Tag scheme: v<versionName> from pahebatcher/build.gradle.kts (currently
#     v0.1.0). The repository had no tags when this scheme was adopted.
#   * If the tag or the release already exists, the job FAILS SAFELY. It never
#     overwrites a release, never moves an existing tag, never replaces assets.
#   * Only the verified APKs, AAB, SHA256SUMS.txt and build metadata are
#     attached. The keystore, .investigation/, .scratch/ and local
#     configuration are never attached.
#
# Explicitly NOT done here: nothing is uploaded to Google Play and no
# push/merge is performed by this file.

name: Release artifacts (merged PR)

on:
  pull_request:
    types: [closed]
    branches: [main]

# Least privilege: this workflow only reads the repository it builds.
permissions:
  contents: read

# Never cancel a run mid-upload; merge runs are kept apart per PR.
concurrency:
  group: release-artifacts-pr-${{ github.event.pull_request.number }}
  cancel-in-progress: false

jobs:
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Verification gates: three INDEPENDENT jobs (job-level granularity so a
  # failed check can be re-run from the Actions UI without re-running the
  # others). Each job checks out the SAME merge commit, validates the wrapper,
  # and sets up the identical toolchain. None of these jobs receives a secret.
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  debug-unit-tests:
    name: Debug unit tests (testDebugUnitTest)
    # Runs only for a MERGED pull request, exactly like the build job - a
    # closed-but-unmerged PR triggers nothing.
    if: github.event.pull_request.merged == true
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 45
    steps:
      - name: Check out the merged commit
        uses: actions/checkout@v7
        with:
          ref: ${{ github.event.pull_request.merge_commit_sha || github.sha }}
          persist-credentials: false

      - name: Validate Gradle wrapper (supply-chain check)
        uses: gradle/actions/wrapper-validation@v6

      # Toolchain mirrors the repository: JDK 25 (gradle.properties /
      # pahebatcher/build.gradle.kts jvmToolchain(25)), Gradle 9.8.2 (wrapper).
      - name: Set up JDK 25
        uses: actions/setup-java@v6
        with:
          distribution: temurin
          java-version: '25'

      # compileSdk 37 -> platforms;android-37.0 (verified via sdkmanager --list),
      # build-tools 36.0.0 matches the locally used build-tools.
      - name: Set up Android SDK
        uses: android-actions/setup-android@v4
        with:
          accept-android-sdk-licenses: true
          packages: 'platform-tools platforms;android-37.0 build-tools;36.0.0'

      - name: Set up Gradle (caching + wrapper reuse)
        uses: gradle/actions/setup-gradle@v6

      # One command, one result, visible on its own in the Actions UI.
      # No secret is provided to this job.
      - name: Run debug unit tests
        run: ./gradlew testDebugUnitTest

  release-unit-tests:
    name: Release unit tests (testReleaseUnitTest)
    if: github.event.pull_request.merged == true
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 45
    steps:
      - name: Check out the merged commit
        uses: actions/checkout@v7
        with:
          ref: ${{ github.event.pull_request.merge_commit_sha || github.sha }}
          persist-credentials: false

      - name: Validate Gradle wrapper (supply-chain check)
        uses: gradle/actions/wrapper-validation@v6

      - name: Set up JDK 25
        uses: actions/setup-java@v6
        with:
          distribution: temurin
          java-version: '25'

      - name: Set up Android SDK
        uses: android-actions/setup-android@v4
        with:
          accept-android-sdk-licenses: true
          packages: 'platform-tools platforms;android-37.0 build-tools;36.0.0'

      - name: Set up Gradle (caching + wrapper reuse)
        uses: gradle/actions/setup-gradle@v6

      # The release variant test task exists because
      # android.onlyEnableUnitTestForTheTestedBuildType=false (gradle.properties).
      # No secret is provided to this job.
      - name: Run release unit tests
        run: ./gradlew testReleaseUnitTest

  debug-lint:
    name: Debug lint (lintDebug)
    if: github.event.pull_request.merged == true
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 45
    steps:
      - name: Check out the merged commit
        uses: actions/checkout@v7
        with:
          ref: ${{ github.event.pull_request.merge_commit_sha || github.sha }}
          persist-credentials: false

      - name: Validate Gradle wrapper (supply-chain check)
        uses: gradle/actions/wrapper-validation@v6

      - name: Set up JDK 25
        uses: actions/setup-java@v6
        with:
          distribution: temurin
          java-version: '25'

      - name: Set up Android SDK
        uses: android-actions/setup-android@v4
        with:
          accept-android-sdk-licenses: true
          packages: 'platform-tools platforms;android-37.0 build-tools;36.0.0'

      - name: Set up Gradle (caching + wrapper reuse)
        uses: gradle/actions/setup-gradle@v6

      # No secret is provided to this job.
      - name: Run debug lint
        run: ./gradlew lintDebug

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Build + verify the per-ABI release APKs, then hand the VERIFIED files to
  # the publish-release job (cache save, not actions/upload-artifact). Only a
  # MERGED pull request reaches this job, and it is one of only two jobs that
  # see signing secrets.
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  build-apks:
    name: Build + verify release APKs
    if: github.event.pull_request.merged == true
    # The three verification gates are the ONLY upstream dependency: no build
    # unless debug tests, release tests and lint all pass.
    needs: [debug-unit-tests, release-unit-tests, debug-lint]
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 60
    # The verified APK signer identity is handed to build-aab (a public
    # certificate digest, never a secret) so the AAB can be checked against the
    # SAME signing identity as the shipped APKs. release_tag is handed to
    # publish-release so the tag is derived from the version actually built.
    outputs:
      signer_digest: ${{ steps.verify-apks.outputs.signer_digest }}
      release_tag: ${{ steps.collect-apks.outputs.release_tag }}
      short_sha: ${{ steps.collect-apks.outputs.short_sha }}
    steps:
      - name: Check out the merged commit
        uses: actions/checkout@v7
        with:
          ref: ${{ github.event.pull_request.merge_commit_sha || github.sha }}
          persist-credentials: false

      # Fail fast BEFORE the build if any signing secret is absent or empty.
      # Only names are echoed; values are never printed and tracing is never
      # enabled around secret-handling steps.
      - name: Validate signing secrets (fail-closed, names only)
        env:
          KS_B64: ${{ secrets.PB_KEYSTORE_BASE64 }}
          KS_PASS: ${{ secrets.PB_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD }}
          KEY_ALIAS: ${{ secrets.PB_KEY_ALIAS }}
          KEY_PASS: ${{ secrets.PB_KEY_PASSWORD }}
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          missing=""
          [ -n "$KS_B64" ]    || missing="${missing} PB_KEYSTORE_BASE64"
          [ -n "$KS_PASS" ]   || missing="${missing} PB_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD"
          [ -n "$KEY_ALIAS" ] || missing="${missing} PB_KEY_ALIAS"
          [ -n "$KEY_PASS" ]  || missing="${missing} PB_KEY_PASSWORD"
          if [ -n "$missing" ]; then
            echo "::error::Missing/empty signing secret(s):${missing}. All four secrets (PB_KEYSTORE_BASE64, PB_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD, PB_KEY_ALIAS, PB_KEY_PASSWORD) must be configured under exactly these names. No fallback exists and no value was printed."
            exit 1
          fi
          echo "All four signing secrets are present (values not echoed)."

      - name: Validate Gradle wrapper (supply-chain check)
        uses: gradle/actions/wrapper-validation@v6

      # Toolchain mirrors the repository: JDK 25 (gradle.properties /
      # pahebatcher/build.gradle.kts jvmToolchain(25)), Gradle 9.8.2 (wrapper).
      - name: Set up JDK 25
        uses: actions/setup-java@v6
        with:
          distribution: temurin
          java-version: '25'

      # compileSdk 37 -> platforms;android-37.0 (verified via sdkmanager --list),
      # build-tools 36.0.0 matches the locally used build-tools.
      - name: Set up Android SDK
        uses: android-actions/setup-android@v4
        with:
          accept-android-sdk-licenses: true
          packages: 'platform-tools platforms;android-37.0 build-tools;36.0.0'

      - name: Set up Gradle (caching + wrapper reuse)
        uses: gradle/actions/setup-gradle@v6

      # Reconstruct the keystore under the runner's temp directory with
      # restrictive permissions. The keystore path is generated here - the
      # owner stores no runner-specific path as a secret. Base64 validity and
      # non-emptiness are checked; password/alias are checked against the
      # keystore itself so a wrong secret fails BEFORE the long build. Output
      # of keytool is discarded; no key material is ever printed.
      - name: Reconstruct release keystore (fail-closed)
        env:
          KS_B64: ${{ secrets.PB_KEYSTORE_BASE64 }}
          KS_PASS: ${{ secrets.PB_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD }}
          KEY_ALIAS: ${{ secrets.PB_KEY_ALIAS }}
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          umask 077
          KS_PATH="${RUNNER_TEMP}/pb-release.keystore"
          if ! printf '%s' "$KS_B64" | base64 -d > "${KS_PATH}"; then
            echo "::error::PB_KEYSTORE_BASE64 is not valid Base64. Refusing to continue."
            rm -f "${KS_PATH}"
            exit 1
          fi
          if [ ! -s "${KS_PATH}" ]; then
            echo "::error::PB_KEYSTORE_BASE64 decoded to an empty file. Refusing to continue."
            rm -f "${KS_PATH}"
            exit 1
          fi
          chmod 600 "${KS_PATH}"
          if ! keytool -list -keystore "${KS_PATH}" -storepass "${KS_PASS}" -alias "${KEY_ALIAS}" > /dev/null; then
            echo "::error::Reconstructed keystore failed validation (wrong PB_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD or PB_KEY_ALIAS, or not a keystore). No value was printed."
            rm -f "${KS_PATH}"
            exit 1
          fi
          echo "PB_RELEASE_KEYSTORE=${KS_PATH}" >> "${GITHUB_ENV}"
          echo "Keystore reconstructed and validated (path is a runner-temp location; contents never printed)."

      # Only this step receives signing secrets, and only the three value
      # secrets - PB_KEYSTORE_BASE64 never reaches the build. The Gradle
      # skeleton (unchanged) signs only when ALL FOUR PB_* variables are
      # present, so a partial set fails closed inside Gradle as well.
      # PB_KEYSTORE_PATH is passed directly (NOT via env.PB_RELEASE_KEYSTORE).
      # A $GITHUB_ENV variable is only visible to LATER STEPS in the same job,
      # and relying on it here is fragile; the explicit runner-temp path is
      # identical to the KS_PATH the reconstruction step just wrote.
      - name: Build release APKs (signed)
        env:
          PB_KEYSTORE_PATH: ${{ runner.temp }}/pb-release.keystore
          PB_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.PB_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD }}
          PB_KEY_ALIAS: ${{ secrets.PB_KEY_ALIAS }}
          PB_KEY_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.PB_KEY_PASSWORD }}
        run: ./gradlew assembleRelease

      # APK-only verification: expected count (2), no unsigned artifacts,
      # apksigner signature validity, identical signer certificate across every
      # APK, and per-ABI native-library purity. No secret is provided here -
      # verification needs none. The verified signer digest is exported for the
      # AAB job.
      - name: Verify APK signatures and ABI packaging
        id: verify-apks
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          BT="${ANDROID_HOME}/build-tools/36.0.0"
          if [ ! -x "${BT}/apksigner" ]; then
            echo "::error::apksigner not found under ${BT}"
            exit 1
          fi
          APK_DIR="pahebatcher/build/outputs/apk/release"

          # A signed AGP build never emits "-unsigned" artifacts; their
          # presence means signing silently did not take effect.
          if ls "${APK_DIR}"/*-unsigned.apk 2>/dev/null | grep -q .; then
            echo "::error::unsigned APK artifact(s) present under ${APK_DIR} - signing did not take effect"
            exit 1
          fi

          shopt -s nullglob
          apks=("${APK_DIR}"/*.apk)
          # splits.abi = reset() + include(arm64-v8a, x86_64), universal off
          # (pahebatcher/build.gradle.kts) => exactly 2 release APKs.
          if [ "${#apks[@]}" -ne 2 ]; then
            echo "::error::expected exactly 2 release APKs (arm64-v8a, x86_64) under ${APK_DIR}, found ${#apks[@]}"
            exit 1
          fi

          reference_digest=""
          seen_abis=""
          # Canonical fingerprint form used by BOTH jobs: bare lowercase hex,
          # exactly 64 characters (32 bytes). Colons and case are normalised
          # away so the AAB job can compare like with like.
          for apk in "${apks[@]}"; do
            name=$(basename "${apk}")
            cert=$("${BT}/apksigner" verify --print-certs "${apk}")
            digest=$(printf '%s\n' "${cert}" \
              | awk '/Signer #1 certificate SHA-256 digest/ {print $NF}' \
              | tr -d ':' | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]' | head -n 1)
            if [ -z "${digest}" ] || ! printf '%s' "${digest}" | grep -Eq '^[0-9a-f]{64}$'; then
              echo "::error::${name}: apksigner reported no valid 64-hex signer certificate SHA-256 digest"
              exit 1
            fi
            if [ -z "${reference_digest}" ]; then
              reference_digest="${digest}"
            elif [ "${digest}" != "${reference_digest}" ]; then
              echo "::error::${name}: signer certificate differs from the other release APKs - inconsistent signing identity"
              exit 1
            fi
            # Expected ABI comes from the artifact name pahebatcher-<abi>-release.apk
            expected_abi=$(printf '%s' "${name}" | sed -n 's/^pahebatcher-\(.*\)-release\.apk$/\1/p')
            if [ -z "${expected_abi}" ]; then
              echo "::error::${name}: does not match the expected pahebatcher-<abi>-release.apk naming"
              exit 1
            fi
            packaged_abis=$(unzip -Z1 "${apk}" | sed -n 's#^lib/\([^/]*\)/.*#\1#p' | sort -u)
            abi_count=$(printf '%s\n' "${packaged_abis}" | grep -c . || true)
            if [ "${abi_count}" -ne 1 ] || [ "${packaged_abis}" != "${expected_abi}" ]; then
              echo "::error::${name}: native libs must contain exactly the '${expected_abi}' ABI, found: $(printf '%s' "${packaged_abis:-<none>}")"
              exit 1
            fi
            seen_abis="${seen_abis}${expected_abi}"$'\n'
            echo "VERIFIED: ${name} signed, signer-sha256=${digest}, single ABI=${expected_abi}"
          done

          # The two APKs must cover exactly the supported ABIs.
          actual_abis=$(printf '%s' "${seen_abis}" | grep -v '^$' | sort -u | tr '\n' ' ' | sed 's/ $//')
          if [ "${actual_abis}" != "arm64-v8a x86_64" ]; then
            echo "::error::release APKs must cover exactly arm64-v8a + x86_64, found: '${actual_abis}'"
            exit 1
          fi

          # Hand the verified signer identity to the AAB job.
          echo "signer_digest=${reference_digest}" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"

      # Checksums + metadata are generated against the APKs actually verified
      # above - the only files this job hands to the publishing job.
      - name: Collect verified APKs, checksums and build metadata
        id: collect-apks
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          mkdir -p dist
          # ABI splits produce one SIGNED APK per ABI (pahebatcher-<abi>-
          # release.apk); collect every one. Defense in depth: never collect an
          # unsigned artifact.
          cp pahebatcher/build/outputs/apk/release/*.apk dist/
          if ls dist/*-unsigned.* 2>/dev/null | grep -q .; then
            echo "::error::unsigned APK reached dist/ - aborting upload"
            exit 1
          fi
          (cd dist && sha256sum ./*.apk > SHA256SUMS.txt)
          version_name=$(sed -n 's/.*versionName = "\([^"]*\)".*/\1/p' pahebatcher/build.gradle.kts | head -n 1)
          version_code=$(sed -n 's/.*versionCode = \([0-9][0-9]*\).*/\1/p' pahebatcher/build.gradle.kts | head -n 1)
          short_sha=$(git rev-parse --short=12 HEAD)
          gradle_version=$(sed -n 's/.*gradle-\([0-9][0-9.]*\)-bin\.zip/\1/p' gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties | head -n 1)
          built_at=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)
          cat > dist/build-metadata.json <<EOF
          {
            "repository": "${GITHUB_REPOSITORY}",
            "commit": "${GITHUB_SHA}",
            "short_commit": "${short_sha}",
            "workflow_run_id": "${GITHUB_RUN_ID}",
            "workflow_run_url": "${GITHUB_SERVER_URL}/${GITHUB_REPOSITORY}/actions/runs/${GITHUB_RUN_ID}",
            "artifact": "apks",
            "variant": "release",
            "signed": true,
            "version_name": "${version_name}",
            "version_code": "${version_code}",
            "gradle": "${gradle_version}",
            "jdk": "25 (temurin)",
            "verification": "testDebugUnitTest + testReleaseUnitTest + lintDebug + apksigner signature and per-ABI checks",
            "built_at_utc": "${built_at}"
          }
          EOF
          artifact_name="PaheBatcher-release-APKs-v${version_name}-code${version_code}-${short_sha}"
          echo "artifact_name=${artifact_name}" >> "$GITHUB_ENV"
          # Handed to publish-release: the deterministic release tag
          # (v<versionName>) and the short commit for the release notes.
          echo "release_tag=v${version_name}" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
          echo "short_sha=${short_sha}" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
          for f in dist/*.apk; do
            echo "APK=$(basename "$f") SHA256=$(sha256sum "$f" | cut -d' ' -f1)"
          done

      # Cross-job handoff of the VERIFIED APKs to publish-release. This is
      # deliberately actions/cache (NOT actions/upload-artifact): the files are
      # keyed to this exact run + attempt, so nothing from another run can be
      # picked up, and a miss is a hard failure downstream rather than a
      # silently empty release. Cache is a transport here, not a distribution
      # channel - the user-facing download surface is the GitHub Release.
      - name: Save verified APKs for the publishing job
        uses: actions/cache/save@v6
        with:
          path: dist
          key: pb-release-apks-${{ github.run_id }}-${{ github.run_attempt }}

      # Unconditional cleanup: the reconstructed keystore is deleted even when
      # any earlier step fails. Never published anywhere.
      - name: Cleanup temporary keystore
        if: always()
        run: |
          rm -f "${RUNNER_TEMP}/pb-release.keystore"
          echo "Temporary keystore removed (if it existed)."

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Build + verify the AAB INDEPENDENTLY. Runs only after build-apks succeeds
  # (so the verified APK signer digest is available as the cross-reference) and
  # uploads the AAB only after its OWN verification passes. If this job fails,
  # the APKs already uploaded by build-apks remain downloadable, and this
  # failure is reported as a genuine failure - it is never masked
  # (no continue-on-error anywhere).
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  build-aab:
    name: Build + verify release AAB
    if: github.event.pull_request.merged == true
    needs: build-apks
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 60
    steps:
      - name: Check out the merged commit
        uses: actions/checkout@v7
        with:
          ref: ${{ github.event.pull_request.merge_commit_sha || github.sha }}
          persist-credentials: false

      - name: Validate signing secrets (fail-closed, names only)
        env:
          KS_B64: ${{ secrets.PB_KEYSTORE_BASE64 }}
          KS_PASS: ${{ secrets.PB_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD }}
          KEY_ALIAS: ${{ secrets.PB_KEY_ALIAS }}
          KEY_PASS: ${{ secrets.PB_KEY_PASSWORD }}
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          missing=""
          [ -n "$KS_B64" ]    || missing="${missing} PB_KEYSTORE_BASE64"
          [ -n "$KS_PASS" ]   || missing="${missing} PB_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD"
          [ -n "$KEY_ALIAS" ] || missing="${missing} PB_KEY_ALIAS"
          [ -n "$KEY_PASS" ]  || missing="${missing} PB_KEY_PASSWORD"
          if [ -n "$missing" ]; then
            echo "::error::Missing/empty signing secret(s):${missing}. All four secrets (PB_KEYSTORE_BASE64, PB_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD, PB_KEY_ALIAS, PB_KEY_PASSWORD) must be configured under exactly these names. No fallback exists and no value was printed."
            exit 1
          fi
          echo "All four signing secrets are present (values not echoed)."

      - name: Validate Gradle wrapper (supply-chain check)
        uses: gradle/actions/wrapper-validation@v6

      - name: Set up JDK 25
        uses: actions/setup-java@v6
        with:
          distribution: temurin
          java-version: '25'

      - name: Set up Android SDK
        uses: android-actions/setup-android@v4
        with:
          accept-android-sdk-licenses: true
          packages: 'platform-tools platforms;android-37.0 build-tools;36.0.0'

      - name: Set up Gradle (caching + wrapper reuse)
        uses: gradle/actions/setup-gradle@v6

      - name: Reconstruct release keystore (fail-closed)
        env:
          KS_B64: ${{ secrets.PB_KEYSTORE_BASE64 }}
          KS_PASS: ${{ secrets.PB_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD }}
          KEY_ALIAS: ${{ secrets.PB_KEY_ALIAS }}
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          umask 077
          KS_PATH="${RUNNER_TEMP}/pb-release.keystore"
          if ! printf '%s' "$KS_B64" | base64 -d > "${KS_PATH}"; then
            echo "::error::PB_KEYSTORE_BASE64 is not valid Base64. Refusing to continue."
            rm -f "${KS_PATH}"
            exit 1
          fi
          if [ ! -s "${KS_PATH}" ]; then
            echo "::error::PB_KEYSTORE_BASE64 decoded to an empty file. Refusing to continue."
            rm -f "${KS_PATH}"
            exit 1
          fi
          chmod 600 "${KS_PATH}"
          if ! keytool -list -keystore "${KS_PATH}" -storepass "${KS_PASS}" -alias "${KEY_ALIAS}" > /dev/null; then
            echo "::error::Reconstructed keystore failed validation (wrong PB_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD or PB_KEY_ALIAS, or not a keystore). No value was printed."
            rm -f "${KS_PATH}"
            exit 1
          fi
          echo "PB_RELEASE_KEYSTORE=${KS_PATH}" >> "${GITHUB_ENV}"
          echo "Keystore reconstructed and validated (path is a runner-temp location; contents never printed)."

      # PB_KEYSTORE_PATH passed directly (same rationale as the APK job):
      # the path is the runner-temp location the reconstruction step wrote,
      # not an env var read back from $GITHUB_ENV.
      - name: Build release AAB (signed)
        env:
          PB_KEYSTORE_PATH: ${{ runner.temp }}/pb-release.keystore
          PB_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.PB_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD }}
          PB_KEY_ALIAS: ${{ secrets.PB_KEY_ALIAS }}
          PB_KEY_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.PB_KEY_PASSWORD }}
        run: ./gradlew bundleRelease

      # AAB-only verification. No secret is provided here.
      #
      # jarsigner -verify (NON-strict) is the INTEGRITY gate and must exit 0; a
      # genuine tamper (digest mismatch) exits 1 and fails this job. The release
      # certificate is intentionally self-signed, so `jarsigner -verify -strict`
      # would exit 4 ("jar verified, with signer errors") for it even though the
      # jar is intact (empirically confirmed on JDK 25) - therefore the -strict
      # output is captured and ECHOED for visibility, but its non-zero
      # self-signed exit is NOT treated as an integrity failure. The signer
      # certificate must still match the verified APKs (keytool digest), and the
      # AAB must package exactly arm64-v8a + x86_64.
      - name: Verify AAB signature, signer identity and ABI packaging
        id: verify-aab
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          AAB_DIR="pahebatcher/build/outputs/bundle/release"
          shopt -s nullglob
          aabs=("${AAB_DIR}"/*.aab)
          if [ "${#aabs[@]}" -ne 1 ]; then
            echo "::error::expected exactly one release AAB under ${AAB_DIR}, found ${#aabs[@]}"
            exit 1
          fi
          aab="${aabs[0]}"
          aab_name=$(basename "${aab}")

          # --- Integrity gate (non-strict): exit 0 required, exit 1 = tamper ---
          set +e
          verify_out=$(jarsigner -verify "${aab}" 2>&1)
          js=$?
          set -e
          if [ "${js}" -ne 0 ]; then
            echo "::error::${aab_name}: jarsigner -verify reported the AAB as NOT verified (exit ${js}) - integrity failure"
            printf '%s\n' "${verify_out}"
            exit 1
          fi
          printf '%s\n' "${verify_out}"

          # --- Surface the -strict diagnostics (self-signed is expected) ---
          set +e
          strict_out=$(jarsigner -verify -strict "${aab}" 2>&1)
          js_strict=$?
          set -e
          printf '%s\n' "${strict_out}"
          if [ "${js_strict}" -ne 0 ]; then
            echo "NOTE: jarsigner -verify -strict exited ${js_strict}; expected for the intentionally self-signed release certificate. The non-strict integrity gate above passed (exit 0)."
          fi

          # --- Same signing identity as the verified APKs ---
          #
          # BUG FIXED: the old extraction searched for "^SHA-256:", but
          # `keytool -printcert -jarfile` on the JDK 25 runner prints the
          # certificate fingerprint label as "SHA256:" (no dash) and
          # INDENTED under "Certificate fingerprints:", so the anchored
          # match never fired, aab_digest came out empty, and the comparison
          # degenerated into "" != "<apk digest>" -> guaranteed false
          # failure (or, worse, a silent pass if both sides were empty).
          #
          # The label is matched without requiring a dash or a line anchor,
          # with optional whitespace, and both fingerprints are normalised to
          # the same canonical form (bare lowercase 64-hex) BEFORE comparison.
          # Each value is then VALIDATED as 64 hex chars so an extraction
          # that yields nothing fails loudly with a clear message instead of
          # comparing an empty string.
          apk_signer="${{ needs.build-apks.outputs.signer_digest }}"
          hex64='^[0-9a-f]{64}$'

          set +e
          cert_dump=$(keytool -printcert -jarfile "${aab}" 2>&1)
          kt=$?
          set -e
          if [ "${kt}" -ne 0 ]; then
            echo "::error::${aab_name}: keytool -printcert -jarfile failed (exit ${kt})"
            printf '%s\n' "${cert_dump}"
            exit 1
          fi

          # Accept "SHA256:" and "SHA-256:" (and any indent/case), take the
          # first fingerprint, strip the byte-separating colons, lowercase.
          aab_digest=$(printf '%s\n' "${cert_dump}" \
            | sed -n 's/^[[:space:]]*SHA-\{0,1\}256:[[:space:]]*\([0-9A-Fa-f:]*\).*/\1/p' \
            | head -n 1 \
            | tr -d ':' | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')
          apk_digest_lc=$(printf '%s' "${apk_signer}" | tr -d ':' | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')

          if [ -z "${aab_digest}" ] || ! printf '%s' "${aab_digest}" | grep -Eq "${hex64}"; then
            echo "::error::${aab_name}: could not extract a valid 64-hex SHA-256 fingerprint from keytool -printcert -jarfile output"
            printf '%s\n' "${cert_dump}"
            exit 1
          fi
          if [ -z "${apk_digest_lc}" ] || ! printf '%s' "${apk_digest_lc}" | grep -Eq "${hex64}"; then
            echo "::error::signer digest handed over from the APK job is not a valid 64-hex SHA-256 fingerprint"
            exit 1
          fi
          if [ "${aab_digest}" != "${apk_digest_lc}" ]; then
            echo "::error::${aab_name}: signer certificate does not match the verified release APKs"
            printf '%s\n' "${cert_dump}"
            exit 1
          fi

          # --- ABI packaging: arm64-v8a + x86_64 only (32-bit pruned) ---
          aab_abis=$(unzip -Z1 "${aab}" | sed -n 's#^base/lib/\([^/]*\)/.*#\1#p' | sort -u)
          expected_aab_abis=$'arm64-v8a\nx86_64'
          if [ "${aab_abis}" != "${expected_aab_abis}" ]; then
            echo "::error::${aab_name}: native libs must declare exactly arm64-v8a + x86_64, found: $(printf '%s' "${aab_abis:-<none>"} | tr '\n' ' ')"
            exit 1
          fi
          echo "VERIFIED: ${aab_name} signed, signer-sha256=${aab_digest}, ABIs=arm64-v8a+x86_64"

      # Checksums + metadata are generated against the AAB actually verified
      # above (the only artifact this job retains/uploads).
      - name: Collect verified AAB, checksums and build metadata
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          mkdir -p dist
          aab=$(ls pahebatcher/build/outputs/bundle/release/*.aab | head -n 1)
          cp "$aab" dist/
          if ls dist/*-unsigned.* 2>/dev/null | grep -q .; then
            echo "::error::unsigned AAB reached dist/ - aborting upload"
            exit 1
          fi
          (cd dist && sha256sum ./*.aab > SHA256SUMS.txt)
          version_name=$(sed -n 's/.*versionName = "\([^"]*\)".*/\1/p' pahebatcher/build.gradle.kts | head -n 1)
          version_code=$(sed -n 's/.*versionCode = \([0-9][0-9]*\).*/\1/p' pahebatcher/build.gradle.kts | head -n 1)
          short_sha=$(git rev-parse --short=12 HEAD)
          gradle_version=$(sed -n 's/.*gradle-\([0-9][0-9.]*\)-bin\.zip/\1/p' gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties | head -n 1)
          built_at=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)
          cat > dist/build-metadata.json <<EOF
          {
            "repository": "${GITHUB_REPOSITORY}",
            "commit": "${GITHUB_SHA}",
            "short_commit": "${short_sha}",
            "workflow_run_id": "${GITHUB_RUN_ID}",
            "workflow_run_url": "${GITHUB_SERVER_URL}/${GITHUB_REPOSITORY}/actions/runs/${GITHUB_RUN_ID}",
            "artifact": "aab",
            "variant": "release",
            "signed": true,
            "version_name": "${version_name}",
            "version_code": "${version_code}",
            "gradle": "${gradle_version}",
            "jdk": "25 (temurin)",
            "verification": "jarsigner integrity (non-strict) + signer match vs APKs + ABI packaging arm64-v8a/x86_64",
            "built_at_utc": "${built_at}"
          }
          EOF
          artifact_name="PaheBatcher-release-AAB-v${version_name}-code${version_code}-${short_sha}"
          echo "artifact_name=${artifact_name}" >> "$GITHUB_ENV"
          echo "AAB=$(basename "$aab") SHA256=$(sha256sum "$aab" | cut -d' ' -f1)"

      # Cross-job handoff of the VERIFIED AAB (cache, never
      # actions/upload-artifact). Runs only after this job's OWN verification
      # succeeded.
      - name: Save verified AAB for the publishing job
        uses: actions/cache/save@v6
        with:
          path: dist
          key: pb-release-aab-${{ github.run_id }}-${{ github.run_attempt }}

      # Unconditional cleanup: the reconstructed keystore is deleted even when
      # any earlier step fails. Never publishes anything.
      - name: Cleanup temporary keystore
        if: always()
        run: |
          rm -f "${RUNNER_TEMP}/pb-release.keystore"
          echo "Temporary keystore removed (if it existed)."

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # PUBLISH - the ONLY job in this workflow holding write permission.
  #
  # `needs:` lists every other job, so publication is structurally impossible
  # unless all three verification gates AND the APK build AND the AAB build
  # succeeded. There is deliberately no APK-only publish path: if build-aab
  # fails, this job never runs and no release is created.
  #
  # This job receives NO signing secret. The only credential it holds is the
  # built-in GITHUB_TOKEN, exposed to `gh` as GH_TOKEN. No personal access
  # token is used.
  #
  # Publishing uses the runner-preinstalled GitHub CLI directly rather than a
  # third-party release action (actions/create-release is archived and was
  # therefore not used).
  #
  # Tag scheme: v<versionName>, taken from the version that was ACTUALLY built
  # and exported by build-apks - not re-parsed here, so the published tag can
  # never drift from the artifacts it describes. The repository had no tags
  # when this scheme was adopted.
  #
  # If the tag or the release already exists, the job fails safely: it never
  # overwrites a release, never moves an existing tag, and never replaces
  # existing release assets.
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  publish-release:
    name: Publish GitHub Release
    if: github.event.pull_request.merged == true
    needs: [debug-unit-tests, release-unit-tests, debug-lint, build-apks, build-aab]
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 15
    # Write access is scoped to THIS job only. Every other job stays read-only.
    permissions:
      contents: write
    steps:
      # fail-on-cache-miss: true - a missing handoff is a hard failure, never
      # an empty or partial release.
      - name: Restore verified APKs
        uses: actions/cache/restore@v6
        with:
          path: dist-apks
          key: pb-release-apks-${{ github.run_id }}-${{ github.run_attempt }}
          fail-on-cache-miss: true

      - name: Restore verified AAB
        uses: actions/cache/restore@v6
        with:
          path: dist-aab
          key: pb-release-aab-${{ github.run_id }}-${{ github.run_attempt }}
          fail-on-cache-miss: true

      # Assemble one payload from the two verified sets, re-checking every
      # checksum so a corrupted or tampered handoff cannot be published, and
      # enforcing an allowlist of file classes.
      - name: Assemble the release payload (verified files only)
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          mkdir -p release

          # 1. Integrity of the handoff: each set must match the checksums
          #    written by its own build job, byte for byte.
          (cd dist-apks && sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt)
          (cd dist-aab  && sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt)

          # 2. Allowlist per set: exactly the expected binaries plus their
          #    checksum + metadata files. Anything unexpected aborts.
          shopt -s nullglob
          apks=(dist-apks/*.apk)
          aabs=(dist-aab/*.aab)
          if [ "${#apks[@]}" -ne 2 ]; then
            echo "::error::expected exactly 2 verified APKs, found ${#apks[@]}"
            exit 1
          fi
          if [ "${#aabs[@]}" -ne 1 ]; then
            echo "::error::expected exactly 1 verified AAB, found ${#aabs[@]}"
            exit 1
          fi
          unexpected=$(find dist-apks dist-aab -type f \
            ! -name '*.apk' ! -name '*.aab' \
            ! -name 'SHA256SUMS.txt' ! -name 'build-metadata.json')
          if [ -n "${unexpected}" ]; then
            echo "::error::unexpected file(s) in the verified payload - refusing to publish:"
            printf '%s\n' "${unexpected}"
            exit 1
          fi
          # Defense in depth: unsigned artifacts must never reach a release.
          if ls dist-apks/*-unsigned.* dist-aab/*-unsigned.* 2>/dev/null | grep -q .; then
            echo "::error::unsigned artifact in the verified payload - refusing to publish"
            exit 1
          fi

          # 3. Build the payload. Only the allowlisted files are copied; the
          #    keystore, .investigation/, .scratch/ and local configuration are
          #    never present in these directories and are never referenced.
          for f in "${apks[@]}"; do cp "$f" release/; done
          cp "${aabs[0]}" release/
          cp dist-apks/build-metadata.json release/apk-build-metadata.json
          cp dist-aab/build-metadata.json   release/aab-build-metadata.json
          (cd release && sha256sum ./*.apk ./*.aab > SHA256SUMS.txt)

          echo "Release payload:"
          (cd release && sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt)
          ls -la release

      # Fail safely if the tag OR the release already exists. `gh` exits
      # non-zero for both probes when the target is absent, which is the only
      # state we proceed from. Nothing is ever overwritten, moved or replaced.
      - name: Refuse to overwrite an existing tag or release
        env:
          GH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
          GH_REPO: ${{ github.repository }}
          TAG: ${{ needs.build-apks.outputs.release_tag }}
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          if [ -z "${TAG}" ]; then
            echo "::error::release tag is empty - refusing to publish"
            exit 1
          fi
          if gh release view "${TAG}" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
            echo "::error::a GitHub Release for '${TAG}' already exists. Refusing to overwrite it or replace its assets."
            exit 1
          fi
          if gh api "repos/${GH_REPO}/git/ref/tags/${TAG}" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
            echo "::error::tag '${TAG}' already exists. Refusing to move it or re-point it at another commit."
            exit 1
          fi
          echo "Tag '${TAG}' and its release are both absent - safe to publish."

      - name: Create the GitHub Release and upload the verified assets
        env:
          GH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
          GH_REPO: ${{ github.repository }}
          TAG: ${{ needs.build-apks.outputs.release_tag }}
          SHORT_SHA: ${{ needs.build-apks.outputs.short_sha }}
          TARGET: ${{ github.event.pull_request.merge_commit_sha || github.sha }}
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          cat > release-notes.md <<EOF
          Signed release assets for PaheBatcher **${TAG}** (commit \`${SHORT_SHA}\`).

          | Asset | Type |
          | --- | --- |
          | \`pahebatcher-arm64-v8a-release.apk\` | Per-ABI release APK |
          | \`pahebatcher-x86_64-release.apk\` | Per-ABI release APK |
          | \`pahebatcher-release.aab\` | Play-ready bundle |
          | \`SHA256SUMS.txt\` | SHA-256 checksums |
          | \`apk-build-metadata.json\` | APK build metadata |
          | \`aab-build-metadata.json\` | AAB build metadata |

          All three binaries were signature-verified before publication: the
          APKs via \`apksigner\` (signature validity, identical signer
          certificate across every split, per-ABI native-library purity) and
          the AAB via \`jarsigner -verify\` plus a signer-certificate match
          against the APKs. \`testDebugUnitTest\`, \`testReleaseUnitTest\` and
          \`lintDebug\` all had to pass first.
          EOF

          gh release create "${TAG}" \
            --repo "${GH_REPO}" \
            --target "${TARGET}" \
            --title "PaheBatcher ${TAG}" \
            --notes-file release-notes.md \
            release/*.apk \
            release/*.aab \
            release/SHA256SUMS.txt \
            release/apk-build-metadata.json \
            release/aab-build-metadata.json

          echo "Published ${TAG} at ${TARGET}"
          gh release view "${TAG}" --repo "${GH_REPO}" \
            --json tagName,assets \
            --jq '"tag=\(.tagName) assets=\(.assets | length)"'
